EXT. HOLLOW BELL TOWER, DROWNED CITY - TWILIGHT

Moss on the stairs. Water laps the third floor. A bronze bell the size of a cart hangs cracked, humming faintly.

QUEEN SABLE VANTHA (40s, armor of woven eel-leather) stands alone beside it, lantern at her feet. She touches the bell with a gloved hand. It hums louder.

SABLE
Count the stairs. Tell me when I'm lying.

Nobody answers. Water laps. She draws her sword.

SABLE (CONT'D)
(to the bell)
I drowned your city. Say it to my face.

The bell hums higher. Behind her, boots on the stairs. She spins, blade level.

Her squire DOBRINA WICK (20s, soaked, nervous) hauls herself up with a coil of rope. Sable lowers the sword an inch.

DOBRINA
Majesty. You said wait below.

SABLE
I said wait. You never listen.

DOBRINA
The water is rising, Majesty. Fast.

SABLE
I know. Get behind me.

Dobrina drops the rope; it uncoils over the edge and plunges. Sable lifts the lantern while Dobrina grabs her sleeve, and the flame bends sideways as the humming swells.

DOBRINA
It's singing at us.

SABLE
It sings when it's afraid.

DOBRINA
Bells aren't afraid, Majesty.

SABLE
This one drowned a city. Be afraid for it.

A crack runs up the bell's flank with a sound like a shot. Sable steps forward, and Dobrina, after one terrified breath, steps with her, and together they lay both hands on the bronze.

SABLE (CONT'D)
Whatever it asks, don't answer.

DOBRINA
What will it ask?

SABLE
Your name. Mine, it already has.

The bronze goes silent. The water stops. Then, from inside the bell, very softly, a child's voice begins to count.
